<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  JawaGroundHulk_Register.xml            Jawa_Patches · authored 2026-08-13
  ============================================================================

  V1 ROW 4, RIDER: the GROUND HULK. The registration half, 3 of 3.

  Defs/PrefabDefs/JawaGroundHulk.xml declares the stamp. Defs/MapGeneration/
  JawaGroundHulk.xml declares the GenStepDef Jawa_StampGroundHulk that places
  it. A GenStepDef on its own runs on NO map; a MapGeneratorDef has to list
  it. This file is that listing, and it is deliberately the same three-file
  shape as JawaResource_Scrapfields.xml, which is already deployed and proven.

  ===========================================================================
  THE TARGET, READ FROM CORE
  ===========================================================================
  C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\RimWorld\Data\Core\Defs\MapGeneration\BasePlayerMapGenerator.xml:4-15

      <MapGeneratorDef ParentName="MapCommonBase" Name="Base_Player">
        <defName>Base_Player</defName>
        <genSteps>
          <li>RocksFromGrid</li>
          <li>ScatterShrines</li>
          ...
        </genSteps>
      </MapGeneratorDef>

  <genSteps> is a PLAIN LIST of GenStepDef names, so <li> is correct here.
  Read from the node, not assumed.

  ===========================================================================
  SCOPE: Base_Player ONLY, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE
  ===========================================================================
  Same call as the scrapfields override, and for a stronger reason. There is
  ONE wreck. The fiction is that this map — the map the clan settles on — is
  where the rest of their own ship came down. Patching the abstract
  MapCommonBase would strew identical hulks across encounter maps, faction
  bases and quest maps, which is not atmosphere, it is a continuity error.

  ===========================================================================
  SAFETY — TWO CONDITIONS, NESTED, AND BOTH ARE LOAD-BEARING
  ===========================================================================
  OUTER tests that Gravship Crashes is present, by testing for the terrain
  it defines:
    C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\workshop\content\294100\3578515873\1.6\Defs\Terrain\Terrain_Foundation.xml:4-5
    packageId Arcjc007.GravshipCrashes (its About\About.xml)

  This mirrors the MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey,Arcjc007.GravshipCrashes"
  on both defs. If either mod is absent, MayRequire drops the GenStepDef at
  load — and adding <li>Jawa_StampGroundHulk</li> to a live genSteps list
  when that def no longer exists is a red error on every map generation.
  🔴 So the two guards must always be changed together. Weakening this one
  turns a clean no-op into a hard failure for anyone without the mod.

  A terrain test can be trusted here regardless of load order: RimWorld
  merges every active mod's Defs into one document FIRST and runs every
  mod's Patches against that merged document afterwards, so the node is
  visible whether Gravship Crashes loads before or after Jawa_Patches.

  INNER test xpath is IDENTICAL to the Add's xpath, so if Core ever renames
  Base_Player or restructures the node this becomes a silent no-op rather
  than a red error. Same discipline as JawaResource_Scrapfields.xml.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/TerrainDef[defName="BrokenSubstructure"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationConditional">
      <xpath>/Defs/MapGeneratorDef[defName="Base_Player"]/genSteps</xpath>
      <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
        <xpath>/Defs/MapGeneratorDef[defName="Base_Player"]/genSteps</xpath>
        <value>
          <li>Jawa_StampGroundHulk</li>
        </value>
      </match>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
